From: RaymondBien <raymond@RaymondBiens-Mac-mini.local>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: aquantia: log how long the firmware upload took

A PHY without a flash of its own gets its firmware over MDIO, one 32-bit
word per three bus writes. For the AQR113C image that is about 276000
writes, done in the probe of the PHY, and every driver probed after it
waits. At the MDC frequency U-Boot leaves on the LS1046A-RDB this took
about 27 seconds of the boot.

Say how long the upload took, so the cost can be read from the kernel
log instead of being guessed from the lines around it.

--- a/drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia_firmware.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia_firmware.c
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 #include <linux/bitfield.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/firmware.h>
+#include <linux/ktime.h>
 #include <linux/crc-itu-t.h>
 #include <linux/nvmem-consumer.h>
 
@@ -154,6 +155,7 @@
 	u32 dram_offset = 0, dram_size = 0;
 	char version[VERSION_STRING_SIZE];
 	u32 primary_offset = 0;
+	ktime_t start;
 	int ret;
 
 	/* extract saved CRC at the end of the fw
@@ -258,6 +260,8 @@
 	phydev_info(phydev, "loading firmware version '%s' from '%s'\n", version,
 		    aqr_fw_src_string[fw_src]);
 
+	start = ktime_get();
+
 	/* stall the microcprocessor */
 	phy_write_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND1, VEND1_GLOBAL_CONTROL2,
 		      VEND1_GLOBAL_CONTROL2_UP_RUN_STALL | VEND1_GLOBAL_CONTROL2_UP_RUN_STALL_OVD);
@@ -276,6 +280,9 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	phydev_info(phydev, "firmware loaded in %lld ms (%u bytes)\n",
+		    ktime_ms_delta(ktime_get(), start), iram_size + dram_size);
+
 	/* make sure soft reset and low power mode are clear */
 	phy_clear_bits_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND1, VEND1_GLOBAL_SC,
 			   VEND1_GLOBAL_SC_SOFT_RESET | VEND1_GLOBAL_SC_LOW_POWER);
